cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, methodology, or published search records, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "SETIsearch: Panchromatic (4.80-Octave, 0.0905-2.515 um) Space-Lyman/FUV/NUV, Optical, Near-IR Echelle Laser, Frequency-Comb, Radio & Photometric Technosignature Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Prospectively locked, reproducible archival searches and pure-stdlib numerical audits
  for panchromatic space Lyman-limit/FUV/NUV (FUSE 0.0905-0.1187 um, HST/COS G130M
  0.1125-0.1450 um, HST/STIS E140M 0.1145-0.1710 um, HST/STIS E230M/E230H 0.1605-0.3150 um),
  ground near-UV (VLT UVES_NUV), optical (HARPS, HARPS-N, ESPRESSO HR/UHR, OHP SOPHIE,
  OHP ELODIE, CFHT ESPaDOnS), far-red (VLT UVES_RED, CARMENES_VIS), near-infrared YJH
  (NIRPS_HE), thermal K-band (VLT CRIRES+), and simultaneous YJHK (CFHT SPIRou APERO
  0.7.295) laser and periodic frequency-comb technosignatures (0.0905-2.515 um, 4.796 octaves
  across 14 spectrographs / 16 arms plus FEROS; 250 unique stars and 1,759 high-resolution
  echelle exposures totaling 569.36 h across V3.0-V4.0 + COMB_V4_1 with Keplerian planetary
  de-Doppler, G4_V40 FUSE dual-channel LiF/SiC & Fiber-B vetoes, 2D CCD/MAMA/COS/H2RG/H4RG
  vetoes, sparse G6 coincidence gating, and uniform all-sky COMB_V4_1 matched filtering across
  100% of D079-D089), unified with planetary-rest-frame 1.4 GHz narrowband radio searches
  (Parkes/GBT) and TESS specular light-sail photometry achieving 23/23 (100%) radio-echelle
  closure across a 250-system multi-messenger synthesis (0 verified ETI detections; 0.0973 W
  HST_STIS Proxima Cen, 0.219 W HST_COS GJ 832, and 0.429 W FUSE Alpha Cen A FUV limits).
